      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "557058:bfcf2b10-5443-4304-afe6-3aff38ddf271",
        "text": "@Joshua Allan Westgard"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "accessLevel": "",
        "id": "5bba58f3eb6f6e2ccfd097c6",
        "text": "@Ben Pennell"
       },
       "type": "mention"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Review Memento, API spec, and Delta documents in order to come up with a design of how versioning and authorization interact in the modeshape impl, as consistent with the relevant specifications.  Identity, answer, or escalate  pertinent questions, such as:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "When resources are versioned, are their ACLs implicitly versioned as well?",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "To what degree are the versions of a resource and the versions of its ACL independent?",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      },
      {
       "content": [
        {
         "content": [
          {
           "text": "Are ACLs for versioned resources immutable?",
           "type": "text"
          }
         ],
         "type": "paragraph"
        }
       ],
       "type": "listItem"
      }
     ],
     "type": "bulletList"
    }
   ],
